From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4.1: prompt encoding for the 1017 checkpoint

Sync vLLM's adapted V4.1 encoder with the reference encoding.py shipped in
deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (rev 1bae0e10):
- reasoning effort low/high/max = 50/75/100, default high = 75 (xhigh removed;
  the tokenizer wrapper still accepts xhigh from old clients as max);
- user messages that only carry tool results do not start a new turn, so the
  current turn keeps its reasoning across tool calls when thinking is dropped;
- tool namespaces: tool/function namespace fields and qualified ns::name.
Checked character-for-character against the checkpoint goldens and reference
by tests/test_dsv41_encoding_1017.py.

diff --git a/vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v41.py b/vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v41.py
index a1449e5..ddcdc0b 100644
--- a/vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v41.py
+++ b/vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v41.py
@@ -76,12 +76,17 @@ def get_deepseek_v41_tokenizer(tokenizer: HfTokenizer) -> HfTokenizer:
                 effort = None
             if effort is None:
                 effort = "high"
+            # The 1017 checkpoint dropped "xhigh" (low/high/max = 50/75/100).
+            # Keep accepting it from existing clients as the next level above
+            # the default instead of rejecting the request.
+            if effort == "xhigh":
+                effort = "max"
             if not (
                 (type(effort) is int and 1 <= effort <= 100)
                 or (isinstance(effort, str) and effort in REASONING_EFFORT_MAPPINGS)
             ):
                 raise ValueError(
-                    "DeepSeek V4.1 reasoning_effort must be low, high, xhigh, max, "
+                    "DeepSeek V4.1 reasoning_effort must be low, high, max, "
                     "or an integer within [1, 100] in chat_template_kwargs"
                 )
 
